  "enhanced_information": "Action potential generation is primarily triggered by the opening of voltage-dependent channels, leading to the propagation of the action potential along the neuron. The subsequent release of neurotransmitters at the presynaptic terminal and binding to postsynaptic receptors result in excitatory or inhibitory responses. The intensity of the stimulus can influence the likelihood of reaching the trigger threshold for action potential generation. Evidence suggests a link between stimulus intensity and functional disorders involving neuropeptide Y interacting with neurons."
